Code Splitting / Chunking /lazy loading/on demand loading/ dynamic import concept in react:

Suppose, you have thousand of components and your bundler load all the components in one file on your browser.That makes your page very very slow,
because that file size has become very huge ,so it is not possible for browser to load. So what should we do? We should do a chunking and a logical bundling.

Lazy loading means:

👉 "Don't load everything at once.
👉 Only load what you need, when you need it."


🧠 Why use Lazy Loading?
When your React app gets bigger, there are lots of components, images, code, etc.
If you load everything together at the start:

a)The app becomes slow to open.
b)The user waits longer.

So here we use lazy loading,
Don't load all screens/components/pages at the beginning.
Only load the parts when the user opens or uses them.

🛍 Example:
Suppose your app has these pages:

🏠 Home

📄 About

🛒 Shop

📞 Contact Us

When the user first opens your app (landing on Home 🏠):

Without lazy loading:
➔ React downloads Home + About + Shop + Contact Us all at once — even though the user is only seeing Home.

With lazy loading:
➔ React downloads ONLY Home.
➔ If the user clicks "Shop," then React downloads Shop page at that moment.

🏃 Simple Real Life Comparison:
Imagine a restaurant 🍔:

Without lazy loading:
They cook every item on the menu before you even order anything.

With lazy loading:
They only cook when you order.

Which one makes more sense? → Of course, cook when ordered = load when needed!

🧠 Why does this matter?
Because:

Your app opens much faster.

You don't waste the user's internet/data downloading things they may never use.

🔥 In super simple words:
"Load it only when the user clicks on it, not before."

So we by using lazy,

Example:
We are using lazy wrapped in Suspense in below example
import "./App.css";
import * as Header from "./Header";
import Body from "./Body";
import Footer from "./Footer";
import {createBrowserRouter, Outlet, RouterProvider} from "react-router-dom"
import AboutComponent from "./Components/AboutComponent";
import Error from "./Components/Error";
import ContactComponent from "./Components/ContactComponent";
import RestaurantMenu from "./Components/RestaurantMenu";
import ProfileComponent from "./Components/ProfileComponent";
import { lazy, Suspense } from "react";
import ShimmerComponent from "./ShimmerComponent";
const Instamart=lazy(()=>import("./Components/Instamart"))
const AppLayout=()=>{
    return(
      <>
      <Header.Header/>
      <Outlet/>
      <Footer/>
      </>
    )
}
const App = () => {

  const AppProvider=createBrowserRouter([
    {
      path:"/",
      element:<AppLayout/>,
      errorElement:<Error/>,
      children:[
        {
          path:"/",
          element:<Body/>
        },
        {
          path:"/about",
          element:<AboutComponent/>,
          children:[{
            path:"profile",
            element:<ProfileComponent/>
          }]
        },
        {
          path:"/contact",
          element:<ContactComponent/>
        },
        {
          path:"/restaurantMenu/:id",
          element:<RestaurantMenu/>
        },
        {
          path:"/instamart",
          element:<Suspense fallback={<ShimmerComponent/>}><Instamart/></Suspense>
        }
      ]
    }
  ])
  return (
    <>
    <RouterProvider router={AppProvider}/>
    </>
  );
};


export default App;
